WEBVTT

00:00:07.665 --> 00:00:09.667
Would you like me
to say a few words?

00:00:09.711 --> 00:00:11.103
Yes.

00:00:11.147 --> 00:00:12.801
He had a family,
I trust?

00:00:12.844 --> 00:00:14.629
Oh, yeah.

00:00:19.721 --> 00:00:21.287
Farewell...

00:00:21.331 --> 00:00:23.507
Aragog.

00:00:25.640 --> 00:00:27.729
[♪♪♪]

00:00:27.772 --> 00:00:30.862
Farewell, Aragog,

00:00:30.906 --> 00:00:34.518
king of the arachnids.

00:00:34.561 --> 00:00:36.694
Your body will decay,

00:00:36.738 --> 00:00:38.348
[DOG HOWLS]

00:00:38.391 --> 00:00:41.438
but your spirit lingers on.

00:00:41.481 --> 00:00:44.789
And your human friends
find solace

00:00:44.833 --> 00:00:48.793
in the loss
they have sustained.

00:00:48.837 --> 00:00:52.144
[SLUGHORN & HAGRID SINGING]

00:00:52.188 --> 00:00:56.583
♪ And it once snapped in two

00:00:56.627 --> 00:01:01.066
♪ Which was sad

00:01:01.110 --> 00:01:03.373
[HAGRID LAUGHING]

00:01:03.416 --> 00:01:05.114
I had him from an egg,
you know.

00:01:05.157 --> 00:01:07.507
Tiny little thing he was
when he hatched.

00:01:07.551 --> 00:01:11.424
No bigger than a Pekinese.
A Pekinese, mind you.

00:01:11.468 --> 00:01:14.514
How sweet.
I once had a fish.

00:01:14.558 --> 00:01:16.734
Francis.
He was very dear to me.

00:01:16.778 --> 00:01:20.651
One afternoon I came downstairs,
and...

00:01:20.695 --> 00:01:22.044
he'd vanished.

00:01:22.087 --> 00:01:23.698
Poof.

00:01:23.741 --> 00:01:27.266
That's very odd, isn't it?It is, isn't it?

00:01:27.310 --> 00:01:30.182
But that's life,
I suppose.

00:01:30.226 --> 00:01:32.184
You-- You go along

00:01:32.228 --> 00:01:36.667
and then suddenly, poof!

00:01:36.711 --> 00:01:38.364
Poof.

00:01:38.408 --> 00:01:41.063
Poof.

00:01:45.067 --> 00:01:47.069
[HAGRID SNORING]

00:01:54.119 --> 00:01:58.950
It was a student
who gave me Francis.

00:01:58.994 --> 00:02:03.999
One spring afternoon
I discovered a bowl on my desk

00:02:04.042 --> 00:02:07.829
with just a few inches
of clear water in it.

00:02:07.872 --> 00:02:11.876
And floating on the surface
was a flower petal.

00:02:12.921 --> 00:02:15.793
As I watched, it sank.

00:02:16.968 --> 00:02:20.015
Just before it reached
the bottom

00:02:20.058 --> 00:02:21.668
it transformed...

00:02:22.844 --> 00:02:25.194
into a wee fish.

00:02:26.325 --> 00:02:29.415
It was beautiful magic.

00:02:29.459 --> 00:02:32.201
Wondrous to behold.

00:02:34.290 --> 00:02:37.467
The flower petal
had come from a lily.

00:02:39.469 --> 00:02:40.775
Your mother.

00:02:42.515 --> 00:02:45.910
The day I came downstairs,

00:02:45.954 --> 00:02:48.739
the day the bowl was empty...

00:02:49.871 --> 00:02:52.438
was the day your mother...

00:02:55.964 --> 00:02:58.401
I know why you're here.

00:03:00.969 --> 00:03:03.362
But I can't help you.

00:03:04.799 --> 00:03:07.279
It would ruin me.

00:03:10.239 --> 00:03:13.198
Do you know why I survived,
professor?

00:03:13.242 --> 00:03:15.635
The night I got this?

00:03:16.854 --> 00:03:19.291
Because of her.

00:03:19.335 --> 00:03:21.380
Because she sacrificed herself.

00:03:21.424 --> 00:03:24.035
Because she refused
to step aside.

00:03:24.079 --> 00:03:27.430
Because her love was
more powerful than Voldemort.

00:03:27.473 --> 00:03:28.735
Don't say his name.

00:03:28.779 --> 00:03:31.521
I'm not afraid of the name,
professor.

00:03:31.564 --> 00:03:35.046
I'm going to tell you something.

00:03:35.090 --> 00:03:38.354
Something others have only
guessed at.

00:03:40.008 --> 00:03:42.097
It's true.

00:03:42.140 --> 00:03:44.447
I am the Chosen One.

00:03:44.490 --> 00:03:46.971
Only I can destroy him,
but in order to do so

00:03:47.015 --> 00:03:49.060
I need to know
what Tom Riddle asked you

00:03:49.104 --> 00:03:50.583
all those years ago
in your office,

00:03:50.627 --> 00:03:53.151
and I need to know
what you told him.

00:03:53.195 --> 00:03:56.198
Be brave, professor.

00:03:57.460 --> 00:04:00.550
Be brave like my mother.

00:04:00.593 --> 00:04:04.467
Otherwise,
you disgrace her.

00:04:04.510 --> 00:04:07.905
Otherwise,
she died for nothing.

00:04:07.949 --> 00:04:11.517
Otherwise, the bowl
will remain empty...

00:04:11.561 --> 00:04:13.389
forever.

00:04:23.747 --> 00:04:26.924
SLUGHORN:
Please, don't think badly of me
when you see it.

00:04:28.708 --> 00:04:32.408
You've no idea what he was like,
even then.

